<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palermo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Panormus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palermo is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, on a bay of the island's north-western coast. Founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> and known to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> as Panormus, it was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabids</a> in 831 and became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Sicily and then of the Norman kingdom, whose first king was crowned there in 1130. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a> revolt began there in 1282.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palermo.jpg" alt="Palermo" width="320" height="349" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tango7174 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sicilia_Palermo5_tango7174.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
